response-og: params[0]: -2.0, params[1]: 3.0, params[2]: -2.0, params[3]: 3.5, params[4]: 0.0
The cart‑position coefficient (w₁ = -2.0) creates a restoring force opposite to the displacement, helping keep the cart centered.  
A positive pole‑angle coefficient (w₂ = 3.0) follows the pattern of the best‑performing policies, providing enough torque to correct small tilts without causing excessive chattering.  
A negative velocity coefficient (w₃ = -2.0) damps cart motion, preventing the accumulation of speed that drives drift.  
A relatively high angular‑velocity gain (w₄ = 3.5) supplies rapid corrective action when the pole starts rotating, improving angular stability.  
The bias term is kept at 0.0 to avoid a constant offset. This combination balances position‑feedback and angle‑feedback while staying within the ±3 N force limits, aiming to extend episode length toward the global optimum.
