The negative weight on cart‑position (p0) will pull the cart back toward the centre when it drifts right, the negative weight on cart‑velocity (p2) damps any residual motion, while the positive weights on pole‑angle (p1) and pole‑angular‑velocity (p3) provide the classic proportional‑derivative feedback that pushes the cart in the direction of the lean to keep the pole upright. A zero bias avoids a constant drift‐inducing offset. This combination directly addresses the right‑ward drift seen in high‑scoring policies while preserving strong angle control, increasing the chance of sustaining the pole for far longer horizons.
